1
00:00:25,219 --> 00:00:28,973
Can this day be any hotter?

2
00:00:31,768 --> 00:00:33,895
We still have to water the crops.

3
00:00:34,604 --> 00:00:36,230
What's that?

4
00:00:36,981 --> 00:00:40,485
I think I hear a water buffalo talking.

5
00:00:41,027 --> 00:00:42,277
So strange.

6
00:00:42,278 --> 00:00:43,654
Why...

7
00:00:44,655 --> 00:00:46,824
Do I sound like a water buffalo?

8
00:00:48,659 --> 00:00:50,953
You look like one.

9
00:00:52,497 --> 00:00:54,874
Stop it. Hey!

10
00:01:00,546 --> 00:01:01,713
So that's what you like?

11
00:01:01,714 --> 00:01:05,051
I'll ride you then.

12
00:01:15,279 --> 00:01:16,487
Water buffalo!

13
00:01:16,511 --> 00:01:18,180
I'll ride you!

14
00:01:32,286 --> 00:01:35,914
- All you think about is your money.
- Can we please lower our voices?

15
00:01:35,915 --> 00:01:39,501
We're in the hospital now.
Your money can wait!

16
00:01:39,502 --> 00:01:40,669
You never pitch in!

17
00:01:40,670 --> 00:01:41,773
Stop it...

18
00:01:41,797 --> 00:01:45,132
Think of the money
for the hospital bills first.

19
00:01:45,133 --> 00:01:46,008
All of you get out!

20
00:01:46,009 --> 00:01:49,136
Lilia, all you do is talk.
What do you even contribute?

21
00:01:49,137 --> 00:01:51,054
You shut up, Camilia.

22
00:01:51,055 --> 00:01:55,475
- I said get out!
- You're too selfish, Lilia.

23
00:01:55,476 --> 00:01:56,811
Stop it.

24
00:01:57,061 --> 00:01:57,854
Lilia...

25
00:01:57,855 --> 00:02:00,439
- Why would I stop?
- Auntie...

26
00:02:01,524 --> 00:02:02,942
Please, Lilia.

27
00:02:03,484 --> 00:02:04,735
Jorge...

28
00:02:06,487 --> 00:02:10,365
Get my card.

29
00:02:10,366 --> 00:02:12,159
Withdraw 50,000 pesos.

30
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:12,910
Okay, Grandpa.

31
00:02:12,911 --> 00:02:15,871
What do you think we should do?

32
00:02:15,872 --> 00:02:18,875
You think of something.

33
00:02:19,876 --> 00:02:22,170
ATM? Okay.

34
00:02:23,921 --> 00:02:28,550
Go ahead, solve our problem.

35
00:02:28,551 --> 00:02:30,802
You're all talk, Lilia.

36
00:02:30,803 --> 00:02:33,431
Think of how you can help out!

37
00:02:46,903 --> 00:02:47,903
Hey.

38
00:02:48,154 --> 00:02:50,489
Why are you still here?

39
00:02:50,823 --> 00:02:54,034
Your parents might be looking for you.

40
00:02:54,035 --> 00:02:55,994
My parents are not here.

41
00:02:55,995 --> 00:02:57,163
And...

42
00:02:59,832 --> 00:03:03,711
- You took my helmet.
- Oh, yeah.

43
00:03:05,421 --> 00:03:06,923
It's okay.

44
00:03:08,549 --> 00:03:11,886
Wanna grab something to eat?

45
00:03:16,390 --> 00:03:18,100
Let's make it quick, okay?

46
00:03:19,018 --> 00:03:23,147
And can we find an ATM nearby?

47
00:03:27,401 --> 00:03:29,111
Hold tight.

48
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:39,500
"All the Things I Leave You"
(Episode 2)

49
00:03:39,956 --> 00:03:41,999
Wait here.

50
00:03:53,636 --> 00:03:56,555
Please sir, don't steal from me.

51
00:04:00,518 --> 00:04:02,644
What do you think of me?

52
00:04:02,645 --> 00:04:04,355
A robber?

53
00:04:04,981 --> 00:04:08,066
I'm too handsome to be a robber.

54
00:04:08,067 --> 00:04:11,653
Do you have to stand so close to me?

55
00:04:11,654 --> 00:04:14,906
I know that you'll be
withdrawing a lot of money.

56
00:04:14,907 --> 00:04:17,617
So I need to stand guard.

57
00:04:17,618 --> 00:04:20,121
We don't know what could happen.

58
00:04:21,372 --> 00:04:23,707
Your call. Whatever.

59
00:04:23,708 --> 00:04:25,960
Continue. I won't look.

60
00:04:28,462 --> 00:04:32,258
1-4-3-4-4...

61
00:04:33,342 --> 00:04:35,469
I love you very much?

62
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:40,891
What?

63
00:04:43,394 --> 00:04:45,228
That's what you said.

64
00:04:45,229 --> 00:04:48,065
I love you very much.

65
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:51,901
I thought you said you won't look.

66
00:04:51,902 --> 00:04:54,363
Yeah but you talk so loud.

67
00:04:57,783 --> 00:05:01,995
1-4-3-4-4.

68
00:05:01,996 --> 00:05:04,831
I-Love-You-Very-Much.

69
00:05:04,832 --> 00:05:06,625
Okay, fine.

70
00:05:10,629 --> 00:05:12,506
You done?

71
00:05:15,801 --> 00:05:17,845
Yeah. Let's go.

72
00:05:58,719 --> 00:06:01,304
Choo-choo...

73
00:06:01,305 --> 00:06:03,724
Open wide.

74
00:06:04,517 --> 00:06:06,351
Can you stop?

75
00:06:06,352 --> 00:06:08,269
I'm not a baby.

76
00:06:08,270 --> 00:06:13,317
I'll treat you like one
if you don't eat your miki.

77
00:06:14,151 --> 00:06:15,736
You're wasting money.

78
00:06:16,237 --> 00:06:18,363
Your choice.

79
00:06:18,364 --> 00:06:22,118
Eat up or I treat you like a baby.

80
00:06:25,454 --> 00:06:27,998
You realize it's hot, right?

81
00:06:29,166 --> 00:06:30,458
Then blow on it.

82
00:06:30,459 --> 00:06:33,712
Do you want me to blow on it?

83
00:06:43,556 --> 00:06:44,932
Jorge.

84
00:06:45,724 --> 00:06:48,351
You're close with your grandpa, aren't you?

85
00:06:48,352 --> 00:06:49,686
Of course.

86
00:06:49,687 --> 00:06:53,983
I'm closer to my grandpa than to my dad.

87
00:06:56,610 --> 00:06:57,695
Why?

88
00:06:58,863 --> 00:06:59,947
No reason.

89
00:07:00,865 --> 00:07:03,242
I just noticed.

90
00:07:06,078 --> 00:07:07,705
What about you?

91
00:07:08,205 --> 00:07:12,959
You said your parents aren't here.

92
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:14,545
Where are they?

93
00:07:16,005 --> 00:07:17,756
They're in Cagayan.

94
00:07:19,758 --> 00:07:20,758
Cagayan?

95
00:07:20,759 --> 00:07:22,470
Yes. Why?

96
00:07:24,763 --> 00:07:27,475
What are you doing here then?

97
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:30,144
I'm with you.

98
00:07:31,979 --> 00:07:33,397
Kidding.

99
00:07:35,232 --> 00:07:36,816
I'm here to work.

100
00:07:36,817 --> 00:07:38,736
You don't study anymore?

101
00:07:39,904 --> 00:07:41,530
I stopped.

102
00:07:43,324 --> 00:07:48,161
I finished high school,
then I needed to work.

103
00:07:48,162 --> 00:07:51,540
How about you?
Where do you study?

104
00:07:55,503 --> 00:07:57,546
I stopped too.

105
00:07:57,922 --> 00:08:01,509
I'm training to manage the restaurant.

106
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:07,890
It's better than going to college.

107
00:08:08,766 --> 00:08:12,936
But I also graduated high school, okay?

108
00:08:12,937 --> 00:08:16,273
So we both stopped studying.

109
00:08:17,441 --> 00:08:18,816
What do they call it again?

110
00:08:18,817 --> 00:08:19,817
Gap...

111
00:08:20,194 --> 00:08:23,280
Gap ban years?

112
00:08:25,491 --> 00:08:27,576
Gap boy years.

113
00:08:28,911 --> 00:08:30,578
Gap boy years?

114
00:08:30,579 --> 00:08:35,292
- Gap year boys.
- Oh! Gap years boys.

115
00:08:38,838 --> 00:08:41,089
Nah.

116
00:08:41,090 --> 00:08:43,007
Mine is a career choice.

117
00:08:43,008 --> 00:08:46,261
- A career choice.
- Wow.

118
00:08:46,262 --> 00:08:48,012
Career choice.

119
00:08:48,013 --> 00:08:50,099
Wish I could say that.

120
00:08:52,142 --> 00:08:53,977
So, we're not the same.

121
00:08:53,978 --> 00:08:55,437
We're different.

122
00:08:56,897 --> 00:09:00,484
If you say so.

123
00:09:04,488 --> 00:09:05,572
Jorge.

124
00:09:05,573 --> 00:09:07,825
I would like to apologize.

125
00:09:08,576 --> 00:09:10,911
I was in a rush this morning.

126
00:09:15,499 --> 00:09:18,543
I wanted to say sorry too.

127
00:09:18,544 --> 00:09:20,588
I was just so angry.

128
00:09:21,297 --> 00:09:23,673
We can forget about it now.

129
00:09:23,674 --> 00:09:25,801
Let's start over.

130
00:09:27,928 --> 00:09:30,096
Okay. Eat more.

131
00:09:30,097 --> 00:09:32,641
Talk less.

132
00:09:53,954 --> 00:09:56,289
Where's grandpa?

133
00:09:56,290 --> 00:09:57,916
What happened to auntie?

134
00:09:59,043 --> 00:10:01,253
She fainted, Jorge.

135
00:10:01,670 --> 00:10:02,671
Why?

136
00:10:02,921 --> 00:10:05,215
Your grandpa's gone.

137
00:10:05,966 --> 00:10:08,510
He's gone.

138
00:10:14,683 --> 00:10:17,393
Jorge!

139
00:10:17,394 --> 00:10:18,394
Nurse!

140
00:10:19,146 --> 00:10:20,229
Jorge.

141
00:10:20,230 --> 00:10:21,230
Nurse.

142
00:10:51,804 --> 00:10:53,846
What happened?

143
00:10:53,847 --> 00:10:55,598
Don't worry, Jorge.

144
00:10:55,599 --> 00:10:57,559
Nothing happened between us.

145
00:10:58,394 --> 00:11:00,561
You fainted last night.

146
00:11:00,562 --> 00:11:02,773
Jorge, let me borrow this.

147
00:11:03,899 --> 00:11:06,609
Am I having a bad dream?

148
00:11:06,610 --> 00:11:08,027
No, Jorge.

149
00:11:08,028 --> 00:11:11,364
What you heard last night was true.

150
00:11:11,365 --> 00:11:13,283
Your grandpa is gone.

151
00:11:14,702 --> 00:11:17,246
My condolences.

152
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:23,585
Sorry, I don't have a shirt
for you to wipe your snot on.

153
00:11:24,336 --> 00:11:27,548
You can do it on my towel.

154
00:11:29,591 --> 00:11:31,343
You're crazy.

155
00:11:31,719 --> 00:11:33,512
Why haven't you gone home?

156
00:11:33,929 --> 00:11:36,055
You fell last night.

157
00:11:36,056 --> 00:11:39,309
You were so heavy
that you hit your head on the stairs.

158
00:11:40,102 --> 00:11:44,772
Your aunt and dad also went
to the funeral parlor.

159
00:11:44,773 --> 00:11:48,193
So they asked me if I
can stay and watch you.

160
00:11:49,027 --> 00:11:52,740
Your aunt and I cleaned earlier too.

161
00:11:55,784 --> 00:11:57,869
It's not a big deal.

162
00:11:57,870 --> 00:11:59,955
The extra cash was nice.

163
00:12:02,207 --> 00:12:05,126
So why are you only wearing a towel?

164
00:12:05,127 --> 00:12:07,170
I just took a shower.

165
00:12:07,171 --> 00:12:11,591
It skipped my mind
that I didn't bring fresh clothes.

166
00:12:11,592 --> 00:12:13,510
My shirt...

167
00:12:13,719 --> 00:12:16,137
You used it to wipe your snot.

168
00:12:16,138 --> 00:12:19,015
So, can I borrow some clothes?

169
00:12:19,016 --> 00:12:21,685
No need, you can stay like that.

170
00:12:23,687 --> 00:12:25,856
You like that?

171
00:12:29,234 --> 00:12:32,570
Wait, let met get a jersey.

172
00:12:32,571 --> 00:12:34,865
Jorge.

173
00:12:36,158 --> 00:12:38,702
Pick a nice jersey, okay?

174
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:44,166
Jorge.

175
00:12:45,459 --> 00:12:47,961
Can't you hand it over nicely, Jorge?

176
00:12:50,047 --> 00:12:52,090
Here it is, boss.

177
00:12:55,093 --> 00:12:58,138
What are you doing?

178
00:13:02,893 --> 00:13:05,312
I already saw it.

179
00:13:10,859 --> 00:13:12,444
Hmmm...

180
00:13:17,991 --> 00:13:18,991
Hmmm...

181
00:13:21,286 --> 00:13:22,286
Hmmm...

182
00:13:23,163 --> 00:13:24,163
But...

183
00:13:24,373 --> 00:13:26,332
You took a shower together, didn't you?

184
00:13:26,333 --> 00:13:28,000
Ruth. Watch your mouth.

185
00:13:28,001 --> 00:13:32,256
What? I'm just asking.

186
00:13:32,589 --> 00:13:35,758
Clean your mind. It's so dirty.

187
00:13:35,759 --> 00:13:36,759
And hey!

188
00:13:37,386 --> 00:13:38,678
For your information,

189
00:13:38,679 --> 00:13:40,472
we did not shower together.

190
00:13:42,641 --> 00:13:44,308
It's good for you to know...

191
00:13:44,309 --> 00:13:48,604
It's forbidden to shower
once the dead body is in the house.

192
00:13:48,605 --> 00:13:52,943
That's what the elders say around here.

193
00:13:57,489 --> 00:13:59,282
But...

194
00:13:59,283 --> 00:14:02,369
You slept together, didn't you?

195
00:14:04,705 --> 00:14:06,247
No!

196
00:14:06,248 --> 00:14:08,876
I slept in the living room.

197
00:14:09,585 --> 00:14:11,879
Really?

198
00:14:13,922 --> 00:14:17,801
Mmm... you two.

199
00:14:20,304 --> 00:14:23,222
So, that's why you're wearing his jersey.

200
00:14:23,223 --> 00:14:24,308
Fine.

201
00:14:25,058 --> 00:14:26,058
Okay.

202
00:14:26,476 --> 00:14:27,852
If you say so.

203
00:14:27,853 --> 00:14:29,896
Jorge.

204
00:14:29,897 --> 00:14:30,897
Kiko.

205
00:14:31,648 --> 00:14:35,444
Hail Mary, full of grace...

206
00:14:41,658 --> 00:14:46,455
Our Father in heaven...

207
00:14:46,997 --> 00:14:51,500
You know, Tino is one of the
kindest people in San Nicolas.

208
00:14:51,501 --> 00:14:53,044
Yes, I remember.

209
00:14:53,045 --> 00:14:54,754
He helped my kid back then.

210
00:14:54,755 --> 00:14:57,883
He's really kind.

211
00:15:18,779 --> 00:15:20,572
Jorge...

212
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:28,330
Do you hear what people are saying
about Grandpa Tino?

213
00:15:29,623 --> 00:15:32,834
Some of them. Why?

214
00:15:33,669 --> 00:15:34,669
No reason.

215
00:15:34,670 --> 00:15:40,550
It seems Boss Tino
was a really good man.

216
00:15:45,931 --> 00:15:48,225
Why are you wearing a black pin?

217
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:53,188
- Yes, that one.
- Why?

218
00:15:54,564 --> 00:15:57,109
In our family,

219
00:15:57,776 --> 00:16:01,446
we only wear it after the funeral.

220
00:16:02,531 --> 00:16:06,243
Different families have different beliefs.

221
00:16:14,751 --> 00:16:16,920
Are you going home?

222
00:16:18,672 --> 00:16:20,798
They say...

223
00:16:20,799 --> 00:16:25,302
You're not allowed to
say goodbye at a wake.

224
00:16:25,303 --> 00:16:27,723
So, you should stay here.

225
00:16:29,141 --> 00:16:31,435
I know that.

226
00:16:32,728 --> 00:16:35,438
Do you want me...

227
00:16:35,439 --> 00:16:38,358
to leave without warning?

228
00:16:40,652 --> 00:16:41,777
Well.

229
00:16:41,778 --> 00:16:44,990
You showed up without warning either.

230
00:16:46,616 --> 00:16:48,117
You're crazy.

231
00:16:48,118 --> 00:16:49,953
You're crazier.

232
00:16:52,539 --> 00:16:54,708
Should I go now?

233
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:59,504
Up to you.

234
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:07,888
Lilia.

235
00:17:08,513 --> 00:17:10,432
Lilia.

236
00:17:11,141 --> 00:17:12,601
Insiong?

237
00:17:13,852 --> 00:17:16,562
Can I ask for a favor?

238
00:17:16,563 --> 00:17:19,191
What now?
You'll borrow money again?

239
00:17:22,903 --> 00:17:25,071
It's for...

240
00:17:25,072 --> 00:17:28,491
Jorge's college.

241
00:17:28,492 --> 00:17:31,202
I want him to finish his studies.

242
00:17:31,203 --> 00:17:36,957
Why would I lend you more money
when you haven't paid what you owe?

243
00:17:36,958 --> 00:17:40,544
You never pay unless I remind you.

244
00:17:40,545 --> 00:17:42,714
Think about it, Insiong.

245
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:45,300
Lilia...

246
00:17:47,386 --> 00:17:49,637
I have a plan.

247
00:17:49,638 --> 00:17:51,890
What is it?

248
00:17:52,599 --> 00:17:54,726
Here it goes.

249
00:17:55,102 --> 00:18:02,984
You'll manage dad's restaurant for now.

250
00:18:03,735 --> 00:18:05,653
I'm the eldest son.

251
00:18:05,654 --> 00:18:09,658
I'm certain that I will
inherit the restaurant.

252
00:18:10,408 --> 00:18:18,408
You can have the restaurant until
I can pay for all the money I borrowed.

253
00:18:19,793 --> 00:18:22,419
I'll agree if we put it in writing.

254
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:25,340
We need a contract for that.

255
00:18:26,550 --> 00:18:28,801
Contract?

256
00:18:28,802 --> 00:18:30,594
Okay.

257
00:18:30,595 --> 00:18:32,680
Let's make it official.

258
00:18:32,681 --> 00:18:36,935
- Until Jorge finishes college.
- Okay. For Jorge.

259
00:18:37,561 --> 00:18:40,313
Okay, I'm good with that.

260
00:18:40,939 --> 00:18:43,150
- Thank you.
- Okay.

261
00:18:49,739 --> 00:18:51,533
Hey, Jorge.

262
00:18:51,908 --> 00:18:53,493
I need to tell you something.

263
00:18:53,618 --> 00:18:57,121
All you do is gossip.
Why don't you help?

264
00:18:57,122 --> 00:18:59,915
I'll help you later.
This is important.

265
00:18:59,916 --> 00:19:03,210
And hey, this is about you...

266
00:19:03,211 --> 00:19:04,754
and the restaurant.

267
00:19:09,885 --> 00:19:14,181
Your Dad and Aunt Lilia
had an agreement.

268
00:19:15,140 --> 00:19:16,683
What?

269
00:19:17,517 --> 00:19:22,062
They're planning to sell the restaurant
so you can continue studying.

270
00:19:22,063 --> 00:19:26,359
They won't give it to you to
manage because they'll sell it.

271
00:19:49,799 --> 00:19:50,800
Dad...

272
00:19:51,092 --> 00:19:52,718
I won't go to college.

273
00:19:52,719 --> 00:19:55,347
Take back what you told Auntie.

274
00:19:58,850 --> 00:20:00,477
Son...

275
00:20:01,186 --> 00:20:03,688
Finish your studies.

276
00:20:04,439 --> 00:20:09,736
Dad, you can't give the restaurant
to Auntie because it's mine.

277
00:20:11,196 --> 00:20:13,280
Yours?

278
00:20:13,281 --> 00:20:14,740
Who...

279
00:20:14,741 --> 00:20:16,785
Who told you that?

280
00:20:17,953 --> 00:20:19,496
Grandpa Tino.

281
00:20:20,330 --> 00:20:22,707
Do you have it on paper?

282
00:20:24,209 --> 00:20:26,168
Do you have proof?

283
00:20:26,169 --> 00:20:29,464
Show it to me.

284
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:34,761
But, Dad...

285
00:20:36,554 --> 00:20:39,391
No more questions.

286
00:20:39,849 --> 00:20:44,104
You will do whatever I say.

287
00:20:48,149 --> 00:20:50,985
You didn't fulfill Grandpa's dream for you.

288
00:20:50,986 --> 00:20:52,736
That's why you're like that.

289
00:20:52,737 --> 00:20:54,823
What?

290
00:20:56,783 --> 00:20:59,911
Insiong, take it easy.

291
00:21:09,588 --> 00:21:11,548
Jorge.

292
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:15,802
Jorge!

293
00:21:40,910 --> 00:21:42,578
What are you doing?

294
00:21:42,579 --> 00:21:44,789
Can I ride with you?

295
00:21:45,332 --> 00:21:47,542
But I'm going home.

296
00:21:48,501 --> 00:21:50,794
Just be with me.

297
00:21:50,795 --> 00:21:52,964
Why? Where are you going?

298
00:21:53,673 --> 00:21:55,300
Don't ask.

299
00:21:55,717 --> 00:21:57,134
Why?

300
00:21:57,135 --> 00:21:59,429
Are you tired of me already?

301
00:22:24,829 --> 00:22:29,084
Hold on tight.
